The '''2025 Baliscan census''' ({{Langx|bl|Censo Baliscano 2025}}) was the 37th {{Linktext|quinquennial}} confederal census. It took place between 27 January and 9 April 2025, and was conducted by the [[Instituto Confederal de Stadística]] (ICS) at an estimated cost of 882 million [[Baliscan sol|sol]]. The census recorded a resident population of 154,556,447 reflecting an increase of 7.7%, over 2020. This was the highest growth rate ever recorded, and the net increase was the highest in history. Additionally, this was the first census since 1918 in which the majority of Balisca's population growth was a result of [[Immigration to Balisca|immigration]]. 

This census's data will be used to determine the allocation of [[Commune district|commune districts]] for the [[2027 Baliscan confederal election]]. 

